/**
 * beatlounge — CHROME localization.
 *
 * Every user-facing UI string (buttons, labels, hints, empty states, toasts,
 * aria-labels) is keyed here and rendered in the user's NATIVE language —
 * `hostApi.getStackConfig().languages[0]` (languages[0] = native, [1..] = the
 * languages being learned). Components call `host.t("key")` (see createHost).
 *
 * MUSIC LOAN-WORDS STAY ENGLISH on purpose — effect names (Reverb, Delay, EQ),
 * note/chord/mode names (Dorian, maqam, raga ids), "BPM", and the like are the
 * international vocabulary of music production; they are NOT keyed here.
 *
 * The `en` object below is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH; `I18nKey` is derived from
 * it (add a key here, get it everywhere, type-checked). All other languages live
 * in the GENERATED_LOCALES block, produced from `en` by `tools/gen_i18n.py`
 * (codex-cli, one call per locale). `t()` collapses regional variants
 * (pt-BR→pt, zh-Hans→zh, ko-polite→ko) and falls back to English per key, so a
 * missing/partial locale never shows blank — it shows clean English.
 */

